The first implementation trims every repeated marker.
```cpp
std::string parse_message(const std::string& input) {
    return trim(input);
}
```

The corrected implementation preserves code blocks and keeps the original source available.
```cpp
std::string parse_message(const std::string& input) {
    auto normalized = normalize_markers(input);
    return trim_preserving_code(normalized);
}
```
